The context window problem"},"438":{"id":"/docs/explanation/chunking-2","page_id":"/docs/explanation/chunking","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/explanation/chunking#how-splitting-works","content":"How splitting works"},"439":{"id":"/docs/explanation/chunking-3","page_id":"/docs/explanation/chunking","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/explanation/chunking#images-and-maximages","content":"Images and `maxImages`"},"440":{"id":"/docs/explanation/chunking-4","page_id":"/docs/explanation/chunking","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/explanation/chunking#why-simple-does-not-chunk","content":"Why `simple` does not chunk"},"441":{"id":"/docs/explanation/chunking-5","page_id":"/docs/explanation/chunking","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/explanation/chunking#merging-partial-results","content":"Merging partial results"},"442":{"id":"/docs/explanation/chunking-6","page_id":"/docs/explanation/chunking","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/explanation/chunking#llm-merge-parallel-doublepass","content":"LLM merge (parallel, doublePass)"},"443":{"id":"/docs/explanation/chunking-7","page_id":"/docs/explanation/chunking","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/explanation/chunking#schema-aware-auto-merge","content":"Schema-aware auto-merge"},"444":{"id":"/docs/explanation/chunking-8","page_id":"/docs/explanation/chunking","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/explanation/chunking#deduplication","content":"Deduplication"},"445":{"id":"/docs/explanation/chunking-9","page_id":"/docs/explanation/chunking","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/explanation/chunking#when-dedup-matters","content":"When dedup matters"},"446":{"id":"/docs/explanation/chunking-10","page_id":"/docs/explanation/chunking","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/explanation/chunking#see-also","content":"See also"},"447":{"id":"/docs/explanation/chunking-11","page_id":"/docs/explanation/chunking","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/explanation/chunking#the-context-window-problem","content":"LLMs have finite context windows. Documents — especially multi-page PDFs, large datasets, or many files at once — often exceed them. Struktur's chunker splits artifact contents into batches that fit within a configurable token budget (`chunkSize`)."},"448":{"id":"/docs/explanation/chunking-12","page_id":"/docs/explanation/chunking","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/explanation/chunking#how-splitting-works","content":"Splitting happens at two levels:"},"449":{"id":"/docs/explanation/chunking-13","page_id":"/docs/explanation/chunking","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/explanation/chunking#how-splitting-works","content":"**ArtifactSplitter:** splits a single large artifact's contents into smaller parts, respecting content slice boundaries (e.g., page boundaries)."},"450":{"id":"/docs/explanation/chunking-14","page_id":"/docs/explanation/chunking","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/explanation/chunking#how-splitting-works","content":"**ArtifactBatcher:** groups artifacts or artifact parts into batches that stay within the token budget and optional image count limit."},"451":{"id":"/docs/explanation/chunking-15","page_id":"/docs/explanation/chunking","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/explanation/chunking#how-splitting-works","content":"The tokenizer uses a character-approximation (not exact token counting). `chunkSize` defaults to 10,000 tokens."},"452":{"id":"/docs/explanation/chunking-16","page_id":"/docs/explanation/chunking","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/explanation/chunking#images-and-maximages","content":"Some strategies accept `maxImages` to cap how many images appear per chunk. This matters when images consume disproportionate context. If a batch would exceed `maxImages`, extra images are moved to the next batch."},"453":{"id":"/docs/explanation/chunking-17","page_id":"/docs/explanation/chunking","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/explanation/chunking#why-simple-does-not-chunk","content":"The `simple` strategy loads all artifacts as-is. If the input exceeds the context window, the LLM call may fail or produce degraded results. For large inputs, use a chunked strategy."},"454":{"id":"/docs/explanation/chunking-18","page_id":"/docs/explanation/chunking","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/explanation/chunking#why-simple-does-not-chunk","content":"This is a deliberate trade-off: `simple` is fast and cheap for small inputs, not suitable for large ones."},"455":{"id":"/docs/explanation/chunking-19","page_id":"/docs/explanation/chunking","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/explanation/chunking#merging-partial-results","content":"When a document is split into N chunks and each chunk is extracted independently, you get N partial objects."},"456":{"id":"/docs/explanation/chunking-20","page_id":"/docs/explanation/chunking","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/explanation/chunking#merging-partial-results","content":"For a scalar-heavy schema (title, author, date), you want the best answer from all chunks."},"457":{"id":"/docs/explanation/chunking-21","page_id":"/docs/explanation/chunking","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/explanation/chunking#merging-partial-results","content":"For an array-heavy schema (line items, product listings), you want to concatenate all arrays and remove duplicates."},"458":{"id":"/docs/explanation/chunking-22","page_id":"/docs/explanation/chunking","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/explanation/chunking#llm-merge-parallel-doublepass","content":"These strategies send all partial results to a **merge model** in a single call, with a prompt asking it to produce a single coherent output. The merge model sees the full schema and all partial outputs."},"459":{"id":"/docs/explanation/chunking-23","page_id":"/docs/explanation/chunking","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/explanation/chunking#llm-merge-parallel-doublepass","content":"This is powerful but costs extra tokens."},"460":{"id":"/docs/explanation/chunking-24","page_id":"/docs/explanation/chunking","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/explanation/chunking#schema-aware-auto-merge","content":"`parallelAutoMerge`, `sequentialAutoMerge`, and `doublePassAutoMerge` use `SmartDataMerger`:"},"461":{"id":"/docs/explanation/chunking-25","page_id":"/docs/explanation/chunking","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/explanation/chunking#schema-aware-auto-merge","content":"**Arrays:** concatenated. `items` from chunk 1 + `items` from chunk 2 = `items` in merged."},"462":{"id":"/docs/explanation/chunking-26","page_id":"/docs/explanation/chunking","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/explanation/chunking#schema-aware-auto-merge","content":"**Objects:** shallow-merged. Keys from later chunks overwrite keys from earlier ones."},"463":{"id":"/docs/explanation/chunking-27","page_id":"/docs/explanation/chunking","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/explanation/chunking#schema-aware-auto-merge","content":"**Scalars:** prefer newer non-empty values."},"464":{"id":"/docs/explanation/chunking-28","page_id":"/docs/explanation/chunking","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/explanation/chunking#schema-aware-auto-merge","content":"This approach avoids an extra LLM call and works well for list-extraction schemas. It does not handle complex cross-chunk synthesis — for that, use LLM merge."},"465":{"id":"/docs/explanation/chunking-29","page_id":"/docs/explanation/chunking","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/explanation/chunking#deduplication","content":"After auto-merging concatenated arrays, there may be duplicates. Dedup runs in two stages:"},"466":{"id":"/docs/explanation/chunking-30","page_id":"/docs/explanation/chunking","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/explanation/chunking#deduplication","content":"**Stage 1: CRC32 hash-based.** Exact duplicates (byte-for-byte identical after stable JSON stringification) are removed without any LLM call. Fast and cheap."},"467":{"id":"/docs/explanation/chunking-31","page_id":"/docs/explanation/chunking","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/explanation/chunking#deduplication","content":"**Stage 2: LLM-based semantic dedup.** A dedupe model is given the merged array and asked to identify semantically equivalent entries (e.g., \"iPhone 15\" vs \"Apple iPhone 15 128GB\"). It returns a list of dot-path keys to remove (e.g., `items.3`)."},"468":{"id":"/docs/explanation/chunking-32","page_id":"/docs/explanation/chunking","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/explanation/chunking#deduplication","content":"Only the auto-merge variants include this step."},"469":{"id":"/docs/explanation/chunking-33","page_id":"/docs/explanation/chunking","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/explanation/chunking#when-dedup-matters","content":"Dedup is valuable when:"},"470":{"id":"/docs/explanation/chunking-34","page_id":"/docs/explanation/chunking","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/explanation/chunking#when-dedup-matters","content":"The same item legitimately appears in multiple chunks."},"471":{"id":"/docs/explanation/chunking-35","page_id":"/docs/explanation/chunking","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/explanation/chunking#when-dedup-matters","content":"The same document segment appears in multiple artifacts."},"472":{"id":"/docs/explanation/chunking-36","page_id":"/docs/explanation/chunking","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/explanation/chunking#when-dedup-matters","content":"Dedup adds token cost and latency. For schemas without arrays, or for inputs with no expected overlap, use strategies without auto-merge."},"473":{"id":"/docs/explanation/chunking-37","page_id":"/docs/explanation/chunking","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/explanation/chunking#see-also","content":"The Extraction Pipeline — the full flow"},"474":{"id":"/docs/explanation/chunking-38","page_id":"/docs/explanation/chunking","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/explanation/chunking#see-also","content":"Strategies — which strategies use chunking"},"475":{"id":"/docs/explanation/chunking-39","page_id":"/docs/explanation/chunking","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/explanation/chunking#see-also","content":"parallel — chunked parallel extraction"},"476":{"id":"/docs/explanation/chunking-40","page_id":"/docs/explanation/chunking","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/explanation/chunking#see-also","content":"sequential — chunked sequential extraction"},"477":{"id":"/docs/explanation","page_id":"/docs/explanation","type":"page","content":"Explanation","breadcrumbs":["Struktur","Concepts"],"tags":[],"url":"/docs/explanation"},"478":{"id":"/docs/explanation-0","page_id":"/docs/explanation","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/explanation#topics","content":"Topics"},"479":{"id":"/docs/explanation-1","page_id":"/docs/explanation","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/explanation","content":"Deep dives into Struktur's architecture, strategies, and design decisions."},"480":{"id":"/docs/explanation-2","page_id":"/docs/explanation","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/explanation#topics","content":"pipeline — How data flows through Struktur"},"481":{"id":"/docs/explanation-3","page_id":"/docs/explanation","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/explanation#topics","content":"chunking — Token-aware document splitting"},"482":{"id":"/docs/explanation-4","page_id":"/docs/explanation","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/explanation#topics","content":"validation — Schema validation and retry logic"},"483":{"id":"/docs/explanation-5","page_id":"/docs/explanation","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/explanation#topics","content":"strategies — Extraction strategies overview"},"484":{"id":"/docs/explanation-6","page_id":"/docs/explanation","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/explanation#topics","content":"preprocessing — Input handling and artifact format"},"485":{"id":"/docs/explanation/pipeline","page_id":"/docs/explanation/pipeline","type":"page","content":"Extraction Lifecycle","breadcrumbs":["Struktur","Concepts"],"tags":[],"url":"/docs/explanation/pipeline"},"486":{"id":"/docs/explanation/pipeline-0","page_id":"/docs/explanation/pipeline","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/explanation/pipeline","content":"How data flows through Struktur from input to output."},"487":{"id":"/docs/explanation/pipeline-1","page_id":"/docs/explanation/pipeline","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/explanation/pipeline#inputs-and-artifacts","content":"Inputs and Artifacts"},"488":{"id":"/docs/explanation/pipeline-2","page_id":"/docs/explanation/pipeline","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/explanation/pipeline#the-strategy-layer","content":"The Strategy layer"},"489":{"id":"/docs/explanation/pipeline-3","page_id":"/docs/explanation/pipeline","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/explanation/pipeline#validation-inside-the-loop","content":"Validation inside the loop"},"490":{"id":"/docs/explanation/pipeline-4","page_id":"/docs/explanation/pipeline","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/explanation/pipeline#the-result","content":"The result"},"491":{"id":"/docs/explanation/pipeline-5","page_id":"/docs/explanation/pipeline","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/explanation/pipeline#see-also","content":"See also"},"492":{"id":"/docs/explanation/pipeline-6","page_id":"/docs/explanation/pipeline","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/explanation/pipeline#inputs-and-artifacts","content":"Struktur operates on **Artifacts**, not raw files. The boundary is intentional — you handle parsing (PDF → text, HTML → markdown), Struktur handles extraction. This keeps the tool focused and lets you use best-of-breed parsers per format."},"493":{"id":"/docs/explanation/pipeline-7","page_id":"/docs/explanation/pipeline","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/explanation/pipeline#inputs-and-artifacts","content":"See Artifacts for the artifact concept."},"494":{"id":"/docs/explanation/pipeline-8","page_id":"/docs/explanation/pipeline","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/explanation/pipeline#the-strategy-layer","content":"A strategy is the orchestration engine. It decides how to split the input, how many LLM calls to make, whether to run them concurrently or sequentially, and how to combine results."},"495":{"id":"/docs/explanation/pipeline-9","page_id":"/docs/explanation/pipeline","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/explanation/pipeline#the-strategy-layer","content":"Built-in strategies cover the common patterns. You can also write your own."},"496":{"id":"/docs/explanation/pipeline-10","page_id":"/docs/explanation/pipeline","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/explanation/pipeline#the-strategy-layer","content":"See Strategies for the strategy concept."},"497":{"id":"/docs/explanation/pipeline-11","page_id":"/docs/explanation/pipeline","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/explanation/pipeline#validation-inside-the-loop","content":"The validation loop is a key differentiator. Every LLM response is validated against the schema using Ajv **before** the strategy considers it done. If validation fails, the errors are serialized and sent back to the model as a follow-up message."},"498":{"id":"/docs/explanation/pipeline-12","page_id":"/docs/explanation/pipeline","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/explanation/pipeline#validation-inside-the-loop","content":"**Smart validation**: For multi-step strategies (parallel, sequential, double-pass), Struktur uses lenient validation during intermediate steps—required field violations are allowed until the final step. This prevents false failures when data is split across chunks. Use the `strict` option to disable this behavior."},"499":{"id":"/docs/explanation/pipeline-13","page_id":"/docs/explanation/pipeline","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/explanation/pipeline#validation-inside-the-loop","content":"Most extractions converge within two attempts. This happens **inside** the strategy, not as a post-processing step."},"500":{"id":"/docs/explanation/pipeline-14","page_id":"/docs/explanation/pipeline","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/explanation/pipeline#validation-inside-the-loop","content":"Default: `maxAttempts` = 3."},"501":{"id":"/docs/explanation/pipeline-15","page_id":"/docs/explanation/pipeline","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/explanation/pipeline#validation-inside-the-loop","content":"See Validation & Retries for the validation concept."},"502":{"id":"/docs/explanation/pipeline-16","page_id":"/docs/explanation/pipeline","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/explanation/pipeline#the-result","content":"The extraction result has three fields:"},"503":{"id":"/docs/explanation/pipeline-17","page_id":"/docs/explanation/pipeline","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/explanation/pipeline#the-result","content":"Field"},"504":{"id":"/docs/explanation/pipeline-18","page_id":"/docs/explanation/pipeline","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/explanation/pipeline#the-result","content":"Description"},"505":{"id":"/docs/explanation/pipeline-19","page_id":"/docs/explanation/pipeline","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/explanation/pipeline#the-result","content":"`data`"},"506":{"id":"/docs/explanation/pipeline-20","page_id":"/docs/explanation/pipeline","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/explanation/pipeline#the-result","content":"Validated output matching your schema. If `error` is set, may not be trustworthy."},"507":{"id":"/docs/explanation/pipeline-21","page_id":"/docs/explanation/pipeline","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/explanation/pipeline#the-result","content":"`usage`"},"508":{"id":"/docs/explanation/pipeline-22","page_id":"/docs/explanation/pipeline","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/explanation/pipeline#the-result","content":"Aggregated token counts across all LLM calls."},"509":{"id":"/docs/explanation/pipeline-23","page_id":"/docs/explanation/pipeline","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/explanation/pipeline#the-result","content":"`error`"},"510":{"id":"/docs/explanation/pipeline-24","page_id":"/docs/explanation/pipeline","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/explanation/pipeline#the-result","content":"Set if extraction encountered a non-fatal error."},"511":{"id":"/docs/explanation/pipeline-25","page_id":"/docs/explanation/pipeline","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/explanation/pipeline#see-also","content":"Artifacts — the input format"},"512":{"id":"/docs/explanation/pipeline-26","page_id":"/docs/explanation/pipeline","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/explanation/pipeline#see-also","content":"Strategies — orchestration patterns"},"513":{"id":"/docs/explanation/pipeline-27","page_id":"/docs/explanation/pipeline","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/explanation/pipeline#see-also","content":"Chunking & Token Budgets — how large documents are split"},"514":{"id":"/docs/explanation/pipeline-28","page_id":"/docs/explanation/pipeline","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/explanation/pipeline#see-also","content":"Validation & Retries — the retry loop"},"515":{"id":"/docs/explanation/preprocessing/artifact-format","page_id":"/docs/explanation/preprocessing/artifact-format","type":"page","content":"Artifact Format","breadcrumbs":["Struktur","Concepts","Document Processing"],"tags":[],"url":"/docs/explanation/preprocessing/artifact-format"},"516":{"id":"/docs/explanation/preprocessing/artifact-format-0","page_id":"/docs/explanation/preprocessing/artifact-format","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/explanation/preprocessing/artifact-format","content":"The artifact abstraction and complete specification."},"517":{"id":"/docs/explanation/preprocessing/artifact-format-1","page_id":"/docs/explanation/preprocessing/artifact-format","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/explanation/preprocessing/artifact-format#the-normalization-boundary","content":"The normalization boundary"},"518":{"id":"/docs/explanation/preprocessing/artifact-format-2","page_id":"/docs/explanation/preprocessing/artifact-format","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/explanation/preprocessing/artifact-format#what-an-artifact-contains","content":"What an artifact contains"},"519":{"id":"/docs/explanation/preprocessing/artifact-format-3","page_id":"/docs/explanation/preprocessing/artifact-format","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/explanation/preprocessing/artifact-format#why-text--images-together","content":"Why text + images together?"},"520":{"id":"/docs/explanation/preprocessing/artifact-format-4","page_id":"/docs/explanation/preprocessing/artifact-format","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/explanation/preprocessing/artifact-format#complete-specification","content":"Complete specification"},"521":{"id":"/docs/explanation/preprocessing/artifact-format-5","page_id":"/docs/explanation/preprocessing/artifact-format","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/explanation/preprocessing/artifact-format#top-level-shape","content":"Top-level shape"},"522":{"id":"/docs/explanation/preprocessing/artifact-format-6","page_id":"/docs/explanation/preprocessing/artifact-format","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/explanation/preprocessing/artifact-format#content-slices","content":"Content slices"},"523":{"id":"/docs/explanation/preprocessing/artifact-format-7","page_id":"/docs/explanation/preprocessing/artifact-format","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/explanation/preprocessing/artifact-format#images","content":"Images"},"524":{"id":"/docs/explanation/preprocessing/artifact-format-8","page_id":"/docs/explanation/preprocessing/artifact-format","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/explanation/preprocessing/artifact-format#complete-example","content":"Complete example"},"525":{"id":"/docs/explanation/preprocessing/artifact-format-9","page_id":"/docs/explanation/preprocessing/artifact-format","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/explanation/preprocessing/artifact-format#validation","content":"Validation"},"526":{"id":"/docs/explanation/preprocessing/artifact-format-10","page_id":"/docs/explanation/preprocessing/artifact-format","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/explanation/preprocessing/artifact-format#built-in-artifact-creation","content":"Built-in artifact creation"},"527":{"id":"/docs/explanation/preprocessing/artifact-format-11","page_id":"/docs/explanation/preprocessing/artifact-format","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/explanation/preprocessing/artifact-format#see-also","content":"See also"},"528":{"id":"/docs/explanation/preprocessing/artifact-format-12","page_id":"/docs/explanation/preprocessing/artifact-format","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/explanation/preprocessing/artifact-format#the-normalization-boundary","content":"Different document types (PDF, HTML, Excel, email) require different parsing strategies. But LLM extraction is the same regardless of source format. The Artifact is the normalized form that crosses that boundary."},"529":{"id":"/docs/explanation/preprocessing/artifact-format-13","page_id":"/docs/explanation/preprocessing/artifact-format","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/explanation/preprocessing/artifact-format#the-normalization-boundary","content":"Struktur only cares about what is in the artifact, not where it came from."},"530":{"id":"/docs/explanation/preprocessing/artifact-format-14","page_id":"/docs/explanation/preprocessing/artifact-format","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/explanation/preprocessing/artifact-format#what-an-artifact-contains","content":"An artifact has:"},"531":{"id":"/docs/explanation/preprocessing/artifact-format-15","page_id":"/docs/explanation/preprocessing/artifact-format","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/explanation/preprocessing/artifact-format#what-an-artifact-contains","content":"`id`: unique identifier"},"532":{"id":"/docs/explanation/preprocessing/artifact-format-16","page_id":"/docs/explanation/preprocessing/artifact-format","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/explanation/preprocessing/artifact-format#what-an-artifact-contains","content":"`type`: type hint (`text`, `image`, `pdf`, `file`)"},"533":{"id":"/docs/explanation/preprocessing/artifact-format-17","page_id":"/docs/explanation/preprocessing/artifact-format","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/explanation/preprocessing/artifact-format#what-an-artifact-contains","content":"`contents`: a sequence of content slices"},"534":{"id":"/docs/explanation/preprocessing/artifact-format-18","page_id":"/docs/explanation/preprocessing/artifact-format","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/explanation/preprocessing/artifact-format#what-an-artifact-contains","content":"Each content slice may have:"},"535":{"id":"/docs/explanation/preprocessing/artifact-format-19","page_id":"/docs/explanation/preprocessing/artifact-format","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/explanation/preprocessing/artifact-format#what-an-artifact-contains","content":"`text`: the text content"},"536":{"id":"/docs/explanation/preprocessing/artifact-format-20","page_id":"/docs/explanation/preprocessing/artifact-format","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/explanation/preprocessing/artifact-format#what-an-artifact-contains","content":"`page`: page number (for paginated documents)"},"537":{"id":"/docs/explanation/preprocessing/artifact-format-21","page_id":"/docs/explanation/preprocessing/artifact-format","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/explanation/preprocessing/artifact-format#what-an-artifact-contains","content":"`media`: embedded images"},"538":{"id":"/docs/explanation/preprocessing/artifact-format-22","page_id":"/docs/explanation/preprocessing/artifact-format","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/explanation/preprocessing/artifact-format#what-an-artifact-contains","content":"This structure naturally maps to paginated documents (each page is a content slice) or segmented text (each paragraph/section is a slice)."},"539":{"id":"/docs/explanation/preprocessing/artifact-format-23","page_id":"/docs/explanation/preprocessing/artifact-format","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/explanation/preprocessing/artifact-format#why-text--images-together","content":"Some documents (real estate exposés, product datasheets) have critical information in images. Because images are embedded directly in content slices alongside text, the LLM sees them in context."},"540":{"id":"/docs/explanation/preprocessing/artifact-format-24","page_id":"/docs/explanation/preprocessing/artifact-format","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/explanation/preprocessing/artifact-format#why-text--images-together","content":"Image limits per chunk are configurable on parallel strategies via `maxImages`."},"541":{"id":"/docs/explanation/preprocessing/artifact-format-25","page_id":"/docs/explanation/preprocessing/artifact-format","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/explanation/preprocessing/artifact-format#top-level-shape","content":"Field"},"542":{"id":"/docs/explanation/preprocessing/artifact-format-26","page_id":"/docs/explanation/preprocessing/artifact-format","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/explanation/preprocessing/artifact-format#top-level-shape","content":"Required"},"543":{"id":"/docs/explanation/preprocessing/artifact-format-27","page_id":"/docs/explanation/preprocessing/artifact-format","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/explanation/preprocessing/artifact-format#top-level-shape","content":"Description"},"544":{"id":"/docs/explanation/preprocessing/artifact-format-28","page_id":"/docs/explanation/preprocessing/artifact-format","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/explanation/preprocessing/artifact-format#top-level-shape","content":"`id`"},"545":{"id":"/docs/explanation/preprocessing/artifact-format-29","page_id":"/docs/explanation/preprocessing/artifact-format","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/explanation/preprocessing/artifact-format#top-level-shape","content":"Yes"},"546":{"id":"/docs/explanation/preprocessing/artifact-format-30","page_id":"/docs/explanation/preprocessing/artifact-format","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/explanation/preprocessing/artifact-format#top-level-shape","content":"Unique identifier"},"547":{"id":"/docs/explanation/preprocessing/artifact-format-31","page_id":"/docs/explanation/preprocessing/artifact-format","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/explanation/preprocessing/artifact-format#top-level-shape","content":"`type`"},"548":{"id":"/docs/ex