,"content":"How the schema validation loop works and why it matters."},"1429":{"id":"/docs/explanation/validation-1","page_id":"/docs/explanation/validation","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/explanation/validation#why-validation-inside-the-loop","content":"Why validation inside the loop?"},"1430":{"id":"/docs/explanation/validation-2","page_id":"/docs/explanation/validation","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/explanation/validation#how-the-retry-loop-works","content":"How the retry loop works"},"1431":{"id":"/docs/explanation/validation-3","page_id":"/docs/explanation/validation","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/explanation/validation#schema-design-affects-retry-rate","content":"Schema design affects retry rate"},"1432":{"id":"/docs/explanation/validation-4","page_id":"/docs/explanation/validation","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/explanation/validation#observing-retries-with-events","content":"Observing retries with events"},"1433":{"id":"/docs/explanation/validation-5","page_id":"/docs/explanation/validation","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/explanation/validation#smart-validation-for-multi-step-strategies","content":"Smart Validation for Multi-Step Strategies"},"1434":{"id":"/docs/explanation/validation-6","page_id":"/docs/explanation/validation","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/explanation/validation#how-smart-validation-works","content":"How smart validation works"},"1435":{"id":"/docs/explanation/validation-7","page_id":"/docs/explanation/validation","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/explanation/validation#opting-into-strict-validation","content":"Opting into strict validation"},"1436":{"id":"/docs/explanation/validation-8","page_id":"/docs/explanation/validation","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/explanation/validation#see-also","content":"See also"},"1437":{"id":"/docs/explanation/validation-9","page_id":"/docs/explanation/validation","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/explanation/validation#why-validation-inside-the-loop","content":"Without in-loop validation, you get JSON that may or may not match your schema. You then have to write error handling, decide whether to retry, and figure out how to feed errors back."},"1438":{"id":"/docs/explanation/validation-10","page_id":"/docs/explanation/validation","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/explanation/validation#why-validation-inside-the-loop","content":"Struktur does all of this for you."},"1439":{"id":"/docs/explanation/validation-11","page_id":"/docs/explanation/validation","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/explanation/validation#how-the-retry-loop-works","content":"Send the extraction prompt to the LLM."},"1440":{"id":"/docs/explanation/validation-12","page_id":"/docs/explanation/validation","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/explanation/validation#how-the-retry-loop-works","content":"Validate the response with Ajv against the schema."},"1441":{"id":"/docs/explanation/validation-13","page_id":"/docs/explanation/validation","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/explanation/validation#how-the-retry-loop-works","content":"If valid: return it."},"1442":{"id":"/docs/explanation/validation-14","page_id":"/docs/explanation/validation","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/explanation/validation#how-the-retry-loop-works","content":"If invalid: serialize the Ajv error array into an XML block, append it to the message thread as a user message, go to step 1."},"1443":{"id":"/docs/explanation/validation-15","page_id":"/docs/explanation/validation","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/explanation/validation#how-the-retry-loop-works","content":"After `maxAttempts` (default 3): throw."},"1444":{"id":"/docs/explanation/validation-16","page_id":"/docs/explanation/validation","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/explanation/validation#how-the-retry-loop-works","content":"The model sees its own mistake and a structured description of it. This self-correction loop is why most extractions converge within 2 attempts."},"1445":{"id":"/docs/explanation/validation-17","page_id":"/docs/explanation/validation","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/explanation/validation#schema-design-affects-retry-rate","content":"Well-constrained schemas fail less often. Tips:"},"1446":{"id":"/docs/explanation/validation-18","page_id":"/docs/explanation/validation","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/explanation/validation#schema-design-affects-retry-rate","content":"Always use `additionalProperties: false`."},"1447":{"id":"/docs/explanation/validation-19","page_id":"/docs/explanation/validation","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/explanation/validation#schema-design-affects-retry-rate","content":"Use `required` arrays explicitly."},"1448":{"id":"/docs/explanation/validation-20","page_id":"/docs/explanation/validation","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/explanation/validation#schema-design-affects-retry-rate","content":"Prefer `enum` for categorical fields."},"1449":{"id":"/docs/explanation/validation-21","page_id":"/docs/explanation/validation","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/explanation/validation#schema-design-affects-retry-rate","content":"Use `format` (e.g., `date`, `email`) only when you need it — it adds validation surface."},"1450":{"id":"/docs/explanation/validation-22","page_id":"/docs/explanation/validation","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/explanation/validation#observing-retries-with-events","content":"Use the `onMessage` event to see when retries happen:"},"1451":{"id":"/docs/explanation/validation-23","page_id":"/docs/explanation/validation","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/explanation/validation#smart-validation-for-multi-step-strategies","content":"When using parallel or sequential strategies, your data might be split across multiple chunks. For example, an invoice's price might appear on page 1, while the vendor name appears on page 5. If both fields are `required` in your schema, validating intermediate results would fail unnecessarily."},"1452":{"id":"/docs/explanation/validation-24","page_id":"/docs/explanation/validation","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/explanation/validation#how-smart-validation-works","content":"Struktur uses **lenient validation** during intermediate extraction steps:"},"1453":{"id":"/docs/explanation/validation-25","page_id":"/docs/explanation/validation","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/explanation/validation#how-smart-validation-works","content":"**Type errors** (`string` vs `number`) → Retry immediately"},"1454":{"id":"/docs/explanation/validation-26","page_id":"/docs/explanation/validation","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/explanation/validation#how-smart-validation-works","content":"**Format errors** (invalid email) → Retry immediately"},"1455":{"id":"/docs/explanation/validation-27","page_id":"/docs/explanation/validation","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/explanation/validation#how-smart-validation-works","content":"**Required field errors** → Allowed during intermediate steps"},"1456":{"id":"/docs/explanation/validation-28","page_id":"/docs/explanation/validation","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/explanation/validation#how-smart-validation-works","content":"**All constraints** → Enforced on final validation"},"1457":{"id":"/docs/explanation/validation-29","page_id":"/docs/explanation/validation","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/explanation/validation#how-smart-validation-works","content":"This means the model can extract partial data without pressure to hallucinate missing required fields. The final validation ensures all required fields are present before returning."},"1458":{"id":"/docs/explanation/validation-30","page_id":"/docs/explanation/validation","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/explanation/validation#opting-into-strict-validation","content":"Disable smart validation with the `strict` flag:"},"1459":{"id":"/docs/explanation/validation-31","page_id":"/docs/explanation/validation","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/explanation/validation#opting-into-strict-validation","content":"Use `strict: true` when:"},"1460":{"id":"/docs/explanation/validation-32","page_id":"/docs/explanation/validation","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/explanation/validation#opting-into-strict-validation","content":"You know each chunk contains complete data"},"1461":{"id":"/docs/explanation/validation-33","page_id":"/docs/explanation/validation","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/explanation/validation#opting-into-strict-validation","content":"You want early failure on missing fields"},"1462":{"id":"/docs/explanation/validation-34","page_id":"/docs/explanation/validation","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/explanation/validation#opting-into-strict-validation","content":"You're debugging extraction issues"},"1463":{"id":"/docs/explanation/validation-35","page_id":"/docs/explanation/validation","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/explanation/validation#see-also","content":"The Extraction Pipeline — where validation fits"},"1464":{"id":"/docs/explanation/validation-36","page_id":"/docs/explanation/validation","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/explanation/validation#see-also","content":"Events & Observability — the events API"},"1465":{"id":"/docs/explanation/validation-37","page_id":"/docs/explanation/validation","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/explanation/validation#see-also","content":"The Artifact Format — schema format"},"1466":{"id":"/docs","page_id":"/docs","type":"page","content":"What is Struktur?","breadcrumbs":["Struktur"],"tags":[],"url":"/docs"},"1467":{"id":"/docs-0","page_id":"/docs","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs","content":"Struktur is a structured data extraction engine that turns pre-parsed documents into validated JSON using LLMs."},"1468":{"id":"/docs-1","page_id":"/docs","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs#why-struktur","content":"Why Struktur?"},"1469":{"id":"/docs-2","page_id":"/docs","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs#a-10-second-demo","content":"A 10-second demo"},"1470":{"id":"/docs-3","page_id":"/docs","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs#what-struktur-is-not","content":"What Struktur is NOT"},"1471":{"id":"/docs-4","page_id":"/docs","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs#who-is-it-for","content":"Who is it for?"},"1472":{"id":"/docs-5","page_id":"/docs","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs#quick-navigation","content":"Quick navigation"},"1473":{"id":"/docs-6","page_id":"/docs","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs","content":"Struktur is a structured data extraction engine that turns pre-parsed documents into validated, schema-typed JSON. It operates on JSON-based artifact DTOs, chunks them by token budgets, runs extraction strategies, validates results with Ajv, and merges or deduplicates outputs where needed."},"1474":{"id":"/docs-7","page_id":"/docs","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs#why-struktur","content":"**Schema-first:** You define the shape, Struktur guarantees it."},"1475":{"id":"/docs-8","page_id":"/docs","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs#why-struktur","content":"**Fields shorthand:** Skip the JSON Schema boilerplate with `--fields \"title, price:number, status:enum{draft|live}\"`."},"1476":{"id":"/docs-9","page_id":"/docs","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs#why-struktur","content":"**Strategy-driven:** From single-shot to double-pass refinement."},"1477":{"id":"/docs-10","page_id":"/docs","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs#why-struktur","content":"**Pipeline-native:** Reads stdin, writes stdout, composes with `jq`."},"1478":{"id":"/docs-11","page_id":"/docs","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs#a-10-second-demo","content":"Expected output:"},"1479":{"id":"/docs-12","page_id":"/docs","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs#what-struktur-is-not","content":"**It does not parse PDFs, HTML, Word docs, or images.** You handle that upstream (e.g. with `markitdown`, `pdftotext`, or your own parser)."},"1480":{"id":"/docs-13","page_id":"/docs","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs#what-struktur-is-not","content":"**It is not a managed API.** It runs