 data extraction engine that turns pre-parsed documents into validated JSON using LLMs."],[1473,"Struktur is a structured data extraction engine that turns pre-parsed documents into validated, schema-typed JSON. It operates on JSON-based artifact DTOs, chunks them by token budgets, runs extraction strategies, validates results with Ajv, and merges or deduplicates outputs where needed."],[529,"Struktur only cares about what is in the artifact, not where it came from."],[492,"Struktur operates on **Artifacts**, not raw files. The boundary is intentional — you handle parsing (PDF → text, HTML → markdown), Struktur handles extraction. This keeps the tool focused and lets you use best-of-breed parsers per format."],[1452,"Struktur uses **lenient validation** during intermediate extraction steps:"],[594,"Struktur validates artifact JSON before processing. Use the CLI:"],[143,"Supported providers: `openai`, `anthropic`, `google`."],[93,"Synopsis"],[179,"Synopsis"],[1626,"Syntax"],[703,"Tesseract, Google Vision, AWS Textract"],[404,"Test a schema against samples"],[1420,"Testing or prototyping"],[649,"Text artifact"],[1552,"Text artifact"],[569,"Text content of this slice"],[624,"Text is split on double newlines into content slices automatically."],[603,"Text/stdin"],[189,"The `--fields` flag (short: `-f`) lets you describe extraction output as a comma-separated string directly on the command line, without writing or maintaining a JSON Schema file."],[1517,"The `--fields` flag builds a JSON Schema on the fly. Each field defaults to `string`; append `:number`, `:integer`, `:bool`, etc. to set the type. See --fields reference for the full syntax."],[1641,"The `fields` parameter lets you describe extraction output as a concise comma-separated string instead of writing a full JSON Schema object. It is designed for quick experiments, CLI one-liners, and any situation where you know the fields you want but don't need schema reuse or complex constraints."],[453,"The `simple` strat